1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:38,309 --> 00:00:39,978
After everything today,

3
00:00:40,645 --> 00:00:44,023
you must be tired. When we get home,
wash up and get some sleep.

4
00:00:47,152 --> 00:00:50,613
Yeah, I'll get some sleep, but…

5
00:00:55,034 --> 00:00:57,078
Speaking of sleep…

6
00:01:01,958 --> 00:01:03,793
When will we start sharing a room again?

7
00:01:05,295 --> 00:01:06,296
What?

8
00:01:07,046 --> 00:01:10,508
I believe that you're my boyfriend now.

9
00:01:10,592 --> 00:01:12,552
I have no choice but to,

10
00:01:14,095 --> 00:01:17,432
and I think I've figured out
why I fell for you.

11
00:01:21,311 --> 00:01:25,523
I know you're being considerate
because I lost my memory,

12
00:01:25,607 --> 00:01:28,443
but what if my memory never returns?

13
00:01:30,361 --> 00:01:33,156
Will we sleep in separate rooms forever?

14
00:01:34,032 --> 00:01:36,409
Like we're just housemates?

15
00:01:44,959 --> 00:01:48,046
I'm saying we should start
getting back to normal.

16
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:50,798
Our plans to get married,

17
00:01:51,382 --> 00:01:52,675
and that we were in love…

18
00:01:54,677 --> 00:01:56,012
I believe it all.

19
00:01:58,306 --> 00:02:00,391
I guess I'm trying to say…

20
00:02:04,145 --> 00:02:07,273
I'd be open to sharing a room

21
00:02:08,274 --> 00:02:09,484
now that I trust you.

22
00:02:18,618 --> 00:02:20,370
Do I need to keep going?

23
00:02:30,421 --> 00:02:32,799
The thing is…

24
00:02:36,928 --> 00:02:40,640
I don't think… we can do that right now.

25
00:02:42,558 --> 00:02:43,476
Why not?

26
00:02:44,352 --> 00:02:46,271
A pleasure to meet you, ma'am!

27
00:02:49,941 --> 00:02:54,362
I'm Kim Gang-rok, Tae-ha's junior.

28
00:02:56,406 --> 00:02:59,742
He came here to settle down
but hasn't found a place yet.

29
00:02:59,826 --> 00:03:01,619
And as you can see, his foot's hurt.

30
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:06,332
So he's staying here with us
until he finds a place?

31
00:03:07,458 --> 00:03:09,752
Yes, I'll only be here for a little while.

32
00:03:09,836 --> 00:03:13,589
Just think of me as your little brother.
I'm at your disposal, whatever you need.

33
00:03:13,673 --> 00:03:17,844
Yeah, and he'll be sharing my room,
so you don't have to worry about a thing.

34
00:03:17,927 --> 00:03:19,137
Yes, I'll be… What?

35
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,513
-What?
-What?

36
00:03:23,308 --> 00:03:26,019
Wouldn't it be better
if you two shared a room

37
00:03:26,102 --> 00:03:28,479
and I slept in a different room?

38
00:03:28,563 --> 00:03:29,939
I think so too.

39
00:03:33,526 --> 00:03:37,613
Still, you're a guest.
It'd be impolite to make you sleep alone.

40
00:03:38,906 --> 00:03:40,533
Since when is that impolite?

41
00:03:41,951 --> 00:03:44,829
Maybe he'll carry you on his back
and sing you a lullaby too.

42
00:03:50,835 --> 00:03:53,588
I don't want to rush into
sharing a room either,

43
00:03:53,671 --> 00:03:55,173
so let's do that, then.

44
00:03:55,673 --> 00:03:57,508
You should sleep with him.

45
00:03:58,009 --> 00:03:59,052
Politely.

46
00:03:59,635 --> 00:04:01,137
Okay, thanks.

47
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:02,221
"Thanks"?

48
00:04:08,561 --> 00:04:09,479
"Thanks"?

49
00:04:12,648 --> 00:04:14,400
Have a good night's…

50
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:18,696
Sir!

51
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:19,947
What? What is it?

52
00:04:20,031 --> 00:04:23,284
Who does he think he is?
Some kind of saint? Confucian scholar?

53
00:04:23,368 --> 00:04:27,163
Why is he so big on politeness,
making sure his guest sleeps well?

54
00:04:30,792 --> 00:04:32,001
So annoying.

55
00:04:36,672 --> 00:04:39,759
Why did I have to bring up sharing a room?

56
00:04:40,551 --> 00:04:43,221
This is so humiliating.

57
00:04:44,764 --> 00:04:47,517
What the heck is wrong with him?

58
00:04:48,851 --> 00:04:49,685
I mean…

59
00:04:50,269 --> 00:04:53,147
I thought you were
supposed to be her boyfriend.

60
00:04:53,231 --> 00:04:56,234
Shouldn't you share a room
with Prosecutor Go to really sell it?

61
00:04:56,317 --> 00:04:57,693
Just lay out the bedding.

62
00:04:57,777 --> 00:05:00,905
I don't understand you. Not one bit.

63
00:05:00,988 --> 00:05:05,451
Putting the act aside,
you like Prosecutor Go, right?

64
00:05:05,535 --> 00:05:08,704
Then, of course,
you should share a room with her.

65
00:05:08,788 --> 00:05:09,872
Why insist on…

66
00:05:13,459 --> 00:05:14,419
Hold up.

67
00:05:16,295 --> 00:05:17,380
Are you shy?

68
00:05:21,342 --> 00:05:22,468
How cute.

69
00:05:25,054 --> 00:05:29,642
I know you're hopeless
when it comes to women,

70
00:05:29,725 --> 00:05:33,563
but I didn't know
you were such a teenager.

71
00:05:36,482 --> 00:05:39,694
Are you not mentally prepared
to share a room just yet?

72
00:05:43,489 --> 00:05:46,451
Is your heart pounding
because she's your first love?

73
00:05:48,327 --> 00:05:50,121
How exactly do you feel?

74
00:05:50,204 --> 00:05:52,123
Are your nerves getting to you?

75
00:05:52,206 --> 00:05:54,375
I wouldn't know. God, this is killing me.

76
00:05:54,459 --> 00:05:55,877
Seriously, I wouldn't know.

77
00:05:56,461 --> 00:05:57,295
Oh, my stomach.

78
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:03,593
Do you want to be shaking with fear?
All over?

79
00:06:04,552 --> 00:06:05,720
I'm sorry.

80
00:06:10,975 --> 00:06:11,809
Well,

81
00:06:12,602 --> 00:06:14,479
good night.

82
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:21,444
But, sir.

83
00:06:22,195 --> 00:06:25,031
Now that she's back,
what are you going to do?

84
00:06:25,114 --> 00:06:27,408
I heard you'll be smuggling her
out of the country.

85
00:06:34,248 --> 00:06:35,416
How do you know that?

86
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:38,753
When you were busy looking for her,
I asked Mr. Hong.

87
00:06:38,836 --> 00:06:41,797
I knew you wouldn't have saved her
without a plan.

88
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:48,679
The boat leaves late this month.

89
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:52,517
Late this month?

90
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,893
I'll send her off then.

91
00:06:53,976 --> 00:06:56,020
If her memory returns by then,

92
00:06:56,103 --> 00:06:58,773
I'm sure she'll leave willingly
to avoid Chairman Baek.

93
00:06:58,856 --> 00:07:00,441
But what if it doesn't?

94
00:07:03,986 --> 00:07:06,697
Then I'll have to force her
to leave the country.

95
00:07:06,781 --> 00:07:08,533
That's the only way she'll be safe.

96
00:07:11,035 --> 00:07:15,373
And let's not call her Prosecutor Go
in this house, even if it's just us.

97
00:07:15,456 --> 00:07:18,042
If she finds out before she remembers,
she'll be at risk.

98
00:07:18,876 --> 00:07:20,545
Yes, understood.

99
00:07:22,004 --> 00:07:22,838
Good night.

100
00:07:30,846 --> 00:07:32,682
Please go on and get some sleep.

101
00:07:32,765 --> 00:07:34,600
I'll be back after a quick smoke.

102
00:07:34,684 --> 00:07:35,726
Okay.

103
00:07:40,273 --> 00:07:41,691
I'll turn off the lights.

104
00:08:21,564 --> 00:08:23,149
Come have breakfast!

105
00:08:26,068 --> 00:08:27,778
You cooked all this by yourself?

106
00:08:27,862 --> 00:08:31,782
I didn't know what you'd like,
so I prepared a variety of cuisines,

107
00:08:31,866 --> 00:08:34,160
from Asia to the Middle East
and even the US.

108
00:08:34,243 --> 00:08:37,121
You won't have to worry about meals
while I'm here.

109
00:08:40,041 --> 00:08:41,042
-Let's eat.
-Okay.

110
00:08:41,626 --> 00:08:42,585
Enjoy your meal!

111
00:08:43,669 --> 00:08:44,670
Looks good.

112
00:08:48,174 --> 00:08:49,008
Of course.

113
00:08:49,091 --> 00:08:51,177
I knew you'd go for that first.

114
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:54,096
I made this for him all the time
when he was hungover.

115
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:56,557
His gochujang stew is great.
You should try it.

116
00:08:59,101 --> 00:09:00,811
I don't really like gochujang.

117
00:09:01,646 --> 00:09:03,022
-I'll have this.
-Sure.

118
00:09:03,105 --> 00:09:05,900
Whatever you eat,
just eat a lot and get better.

119
00:09:05,983 --> 00:09:08,653
-And I hope your clinic visit goes well.
-Clinic visit?

120
00:09:09,654 --> 00:09:12,156
Don't you get treatment
on Tuesdays and Fridays?

121
00:09:13,157 --> 00:09:14,825
Did Mr. Hong tell you that too?

122
00:09:16,369 --> 00:09:19,538
I've been your right-hand man
for ten years now.

123
00:09:19,622 --> 00:09:22,083
Keeping tabs on your schedule is a given.

124
00:09:23,334 --> 00:09:28,339
Eat up, and good luck
with your treatment today.

125
00:09:39,266 --> 00:09:40,851
If I remember correctly,

126
00:09:40,935 --> 00:09:44,814
the last time you two were here,
you had a big argument and then left.

127
00:09:44,897 --> 00:09:47,692
I take it things have changed
quite a bit since then?

128
00:09:48,526 --> 00:09:51,487
I haven't regained my memory,
but I guess you could say

129
00:09:52,446 --> 00:09:54,198
I regained my trust in him.

130
00:09:54,281 --> 00:09:55,783
Trust? I see.

131
00:09:57,785 --> 00:10:00,413
Isn't that just how things go
between a man and a woman?

132
00:10:06,419 --> 00:10:09,046
Let's go ahead with the treatment
as planned.

133
00:10:09,130 --> 00:10:11,215
You mentioned physical therapy,
didn't you?

134
00:10:11,298 --> 00:10:12,133
Yes, I did.

135
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:16,512
It's called TMS, and we use
magnetic pulses on the cerebral cortex,

136
00:10:16,595 --> 00:10:18,139
which stores long-term memory.

137
00:10:18,222 --> 00:10:20,599
If we're lucky,
it will stimulate the area,

138
00:10:20,683 --> 00:10:22,184
and her memory will come back.

139
00:10:22,268 --> 00:10:25,813
Is it painful, by any chance?
Might it cause severe headaches or--

140
00:10:25,896 --> 00:10:28,941
Remember when our teacher whacked you
for picking A's in the multiple choice?

141
00:10:29,608 --> 00:10:31,360
It'll hurt less than that.

142
00:10:37,032 --> 00:10:39,118
So, TMS first, then…

143
00:10:40,453 --> 00:10:41,912
TMS TREATMENT ROOM

144
00:10:41,996 --> 00:10:45,666
You were a mess, saying you were scared
and couldn't believe him and whatnot.

145
00:10:45,750 --> 00:10:49,462
Women sure are hard to read.

146
00:10:51,505 --> 00:10:53,382
Well, things happened.

147
00:10:53,966 --> 00:10:56,010
I believe everything Jang Tae-ha says now.

148
00:10:57,178 --> 00:10:59,305
Then why bother with
getting your memory back?

149
00:11:02,433 --> 00:11:04,685
Because I want to remember our past.

150
00:11:05,853 --> 00:11:08,689
I think it's true
that my life was nothing special,

151
00:11:09,690 --> 00:11:13,194
but Jang Tae-ha
seems to have liked me a lot regardless.

152
00:11:13,277 --> 00:11:16,030
Right now, only he remembers that.

153
00:11:16,113 --> 00:11:17,615
How lonely must that be?

154
00:11:17,698 --> 00:11:22,036
Not being able to share the memories
you made with the person you love.

155
00:11:26,832 --> 00:11:29,752
-Was it okay?
-Yeah, I didn't feel a thing.

156
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:32,254
Here.

157
00:11:32,338 --> 00:11:33,172
Thanks.

158
00:11:33,756 --> 00:11:34,632
Don't mention it.

159
00:11:36,258 --> 00:11:37,301
We'll get going.

160
00:11:38,761 --> 00:11:39,887
Let's go.

161
00:11:54,985 --> 00:11:56,278
Ms. Lee Chae-yeon.

162
00:11:56,362 --> 00:11:57,488
Yes.

163
00:12:03,285 --> 00:12:05,371
That woman who was your classmate.

164
00:12:06,038 --> 00:12:07,456
I have a bad feeling about her.

165
00:12:07,957 --> 00:12:08,791
Why?

166
00:12:08,874 --> 00:12:13,546
Women can easily sniff out other women
who are interested in their men.

167
00:12:14,129 --> 00:12:17,299
The way she defended you
and had a go at me last time.

168
00:12:17,383 --> 00:12:20,052
And the way she looks at you.

169
00:12:23,347 --> 00:12:24,640
Why are you laughing?

170
00:12:25,474 --> 00:12:27,977
Could it be that she likes you?

171
00:12:29,019 --> 00:12:30,729
-No way.
-What do you mean "no way"?

172
00:12:30,813 --> 00:12:33,524
Didn't you see her earlier?
She was doing all this.

173
00:12:34,108 --> 00:12:36,610
Her hair was already tucked
behind her ear.

174
00:12:36,694 --> 00:12:40,197
There was no hair left to tuck,
but she kept doing this.

175
00:12:40,781 --> 00:12:45,661
That's a subconscious way of flirting
to show off her femininity and neckline.

176
00:12:46,704 --> 00:12:49,123
Let's go to the gym.
Mr. Hong's treating us to shrimp.

177
00:12:58,257 --> 00:13:02,386
-Is the treatment she got today effective?
-Thank you.

178
00:13:02,469 --> 00:13:05,890
They can't guarantee anything.
We can only hope for the best.

179
00:13:05,973 --> 00:13:07,057
Sure.

180
00:13:14,189 --> 00:13:15,524
That shrimp's gonna freeze.

181
00:13:21,864 --> 00:13:23,699
-Eat up.
-Okay.

182
00:13:24,909 --> 00:13:29,246
You're really living up to your reputation
as the village romantic.

183
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:30,873
As if you're the only lovebirds.

184
00:13:31,874 --> 00:13:32,917
We're lovebirds too.

185
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,545
-Here.
-Open up.

186
00:13:41,258 --> 00:13:43,344
Is this a village of love?

187
00:13:44,887 --> 00:13:47,640
I have shrimp whiskers
stuck under my nails

188
00:13:47,723 --> 00:13:51,101
from peeling and eating shrimp
all by my lonesome self.

189
00:13:52,728 --> 00:13:54,188
Here, eat up.

190
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,106
Thank you.

191
00:13:56,732 --> 00:13:57,650
Thanks.

192
00:13:58,692 --> 00:13:59,568
-Hilarious.
-Thanks.

193
00:14:03,155 --> 00:14:06,659
Please go on and get some sleep.
I'll be back after a quick smoke.

194
00:14:08,118 --> 00:14:09,078
So funny.

195
00:14:09,745 --> 00:14:10,704
Thank you.

196
00:14:11,830 --> 00:14:14,583
Is today the day the car will be ready?

197
00:14:16,794 --> 00:14:19,797
Sorry? Yes, it'll be ready today.

198
00:14:20,381 --> 00:14:23,175
He says he bought a good one
to drive you around in.

199
00:14:27,012 --> 00:14:28,430
Shall we pick it up together?

200
00:14:30,724 --> 00:14:31,850
No, thanks.

201
00:14:31,934 --> 00:14:35,396
You're doing all that for me,
so I want to earn my keep.

202
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:37,064
Earn your keep?

203
00:14:37,147 --> 00:14:39,274
You said I worked
at your grandma's taffy shop.

204
00:14:39,942 --> 00:14:41,819
I should go back to my old job.

205
00:14:42,319 --> 00:14:44,655
I bet I could learn the ropes
pretty quickly.

206
00:14:46,115 --> 00:14:47,533
It didn't look too difficult.

207
00:14:48,075 --> 00:14:50,035
You want me to do all this?

208
00:14:53,664 --> 00:14:55,457
All you have to do is scoop and pour.

209
00:14:55,541 --> 00:14:57,918
What's so hard about that?

210
00:14:58,669 --> 00:15:00,045
Try it.

211
00:15:00,129 --> 00:15:02,965
Do you have any thick gloves I could …

212
00:15:09,346 --> 00:15:10,973
-Grab it already.
-Yes, ma'am.

213
00:15:11,056 --> 00:15:13,559
Such a neat freak.

214
00:15:15,561 --> 00:15:17,021
It's hot!

215
00:15:18,147 --> 00:15:20,524
-Did you burn yourself?
-No, I'm okay.

216
00:15:20,607 --> 00:15:22,067
What should I do?

217
00:15:22,151 --> 00:15:23,152
Oh no.

218
00:15:23,235 --> 00:15:26,405
I'm sorry. Do you have another one?

219
00:15:28,532 --> 00:15:30,159
Do you have a ladle or something?

220
00:15:30,242 --> 00:15:32,953
The taffy would stick to something
like that.

221
00:15:33,037 --> 00:15:37,124
You need to use a lacquered bowl
so the taffy can slide right off!

222
00:15:37,916 --> 00:15:40,085
So there's a reason for everything.

223
00:15:40,669 --> 00:15:41,503
I'm so sorry.

224
00:15:41,587 --> 00:15:44,798
If your hand's okay,
go outside and ask around for a bowl.

225
00:15:53,557 --> 00:15:55,684
That should be enough to dull them, right?

226
00:16:02,483 --> 00:16:05,611
I'm definitely going to cut myself.

227
00:16:06,111 --> 00:16:07,654
Good grief.

228
00:16:08,781 --> 00:16:12,868
Why did my spiritual powers
have to just up and disappear?

229
00:16:14,161 --> 00:16:16,413
My spiritual powers are gone,

230
00:16:16,997 --> 00:16:20,501
and soon my feet will be gone too.

231
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,764
What is she doing here?
How long has she been there?

232
00:16:34,389 --> 00:16:36,517
Did she hear everything?

233
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,685
I need to borrow a gourd bowl.

234
00:16:38,769 --> 00:16:39,645
What?

235
00:16:39,728 --> 00:16:41,021
A gourd bowl.

236
00:16:41,772 --> 00:16:43,982
Right, a gourd bowl.

237
00:16:46,401 --> 00:16:47,569
Yeah, okay.

238
00:16:48,821 --> 00:16:51,949
GARAK SHAMAN

239
00:16:52,032 --> 00:16:52,866
What the heck?

240
00:16:53,367 --> 00:16:55,494
So she really doesn't have
spiritual powers.

241
00:16:57,246 --> 00:16:59,206
AN MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

242
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:00,999
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

243
00:17:01,083 --> 00:17:04,294
I'll work on the handover,
so find my replacement as soon as you can.

244
00:17:04,378 --> 00:17:05,629
You're really doing this?

245
00:17:05,712 --> 00:17:07,673
How can we work together
after breaking up?

246
00:17:07,756 --> 00:17:09,716
-Hey, Min Su-ji.
-Yeah, what?

247
00:17:14,805 --> 00:17:18,100
Do you even have somewhere to go
if you quit?

248
00:17:21,603 --> 00:17:22,938
I'll figure something out.

249
00:17:32,406 --> 00:17:35,450
That's not what I meant.
Why do I keep saying things like that?

250
00:17:36,368 --> 00:17:37,703
Damn it.

251
00:17:42,124 --> 00:17:45,586
What? Well, look who it is! It's Su-ji!

252
00:17:45,669 --> 00:17:47,588
-Have you been well?
-Of course!

253
00:17:47,671 --> 00:17:49,756
What brings you to Taffy Village?

254
00:17:50,424 --> 00:17:51,925
I just thought I'd stop by.

255
00:17:52,009 --> 00:17:54,178
Can I get a kimchi stew
and a bottle of soju?

256
00:17:54,261 --> 00:17:55,596
Of course.

257
00:17:58,348 --> 00:18:02,728
Feels like yesterday you were in uniform.
Now you're old enough to drink?

258
00:18:02,811 --> 00:18:03,937
Oh, aren't you pretty!

259
00:18:04,021 --> 00:18:06,231
Su-ji, you're old enough
to get married now.

260
00:18:06,315 --> 00:18:10,110
What's with the marriage talk
from the get-go?

261
00:18:10,194 --> 00:18:12,112
Are you happy because you're married?

262
00:18:13,864 --> 00:18:18,243
Didn't you say that night at the motel
near Gujin rotary with Pil-seung's father

263
00:18:18,327 --> 00:18:20,370
was the biggest mistake of your life?

264
00:18:20,454 --> 00:18:22,497
Su-ji, don't you ever get married.

265
00:18:22,581 --> 00:18:24,333
But still,

266
00:18:24,416 --> 00:18:27,336
if everyone's married,
and you're the only one left,

267
00:18:27,419 --> 00:18:28,921
it would get lonely.

268
00:18:29,004 --> 00:18:30,005
I guess you're right.

269
00:18:30,088 --> 00:18:33,133
Come to think of it,
aren't you the same age as Tae-ha?

270
00:18:33,217 --> 00:18:34,885
-That's right.
-Yeah.

271
00:18:34,968 --> 00:18:37,679
Tae-ha brought home a wife he adores
and started a family.

272
00:18:38,764 --> 00:18:41,183
-Su-ji, don't you have anyone?
-Don't you?

273
00:18:42,643 --> 00:18:44,478
No, I don't.

274
00:18:49,524 --> 00:18:51,735
Have a drink. Go on.

275
00:19:16,843 --> 00:19:19,096
WALNUTS
BOOSTS BRAIN HEALTH AND MEMORY

276
00:19:19,179 --> 00:19:20,347
Thank you.

277
00:19:20,430 --> 00:19:21,807
Su-ji, will you be okay?

278
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:24,935
-I'm totally fine. I swear.
-Goodness, I'm worried.

279
00:19:25,018 --> 00:19:26,603
-I'll get going.
-Careful now.

280
00:19:26,687 --> 00:19:28,105
Will you be okay?

281
00:19:31,191 --> 00:19:32,943
Jang Tae-ha.

282
00:19:41,743 --> 00:19:42,577
You're…

283
00:19:42,661 --> 00:19:45,914
Su-ji. Min Su-ji.

284
00:19:45,998 --> 00:19:47,874
Don't you dare call me Sun-deok again.

285
00:19:48,667 --> 00:19:49,501
Right.

286
00:19:51,795 --> 00:19:52,629
Are you okay?

287
00:19:52,713 --> 00:19:54,464
If I'm not okay,

288
00:19:55,465 --> 00:19:56,675
will you take me home?

289
00:19:59,136 --> 00:19:59,970
Look at that.

290
00:20:01,722 --> 00:20:03,890
I have to get home.

291
00:20:05,183 --> 00:20:06,268
Right, Gi-jun.

292
00:20:07,019 --> 00:20:09,271
You work with Gi-jun, don't you? Hold on.

293
00:20:12,482 --> 00:20:13,775
She grabbed his hand!

294
00:20:14,609 --> 00:20:15,902
Don't.

295
00:20:15,986 --> 00:20:16,820
What?

296
00:20:16,903 --> 00:20:19,531
I'm saying don't call him.

297
00:20:26,747 --> 00:20:28,540
If I were your girlfriend,

298
00:20:29,916 --> 00:20:32,169
could I have been loved too?

299
00:20:35,130 --> 00:20:36,048
Stop right there.

300
00:20:38,050 --> 00:20:39,885
-What is it?
-Eun-sae's here.

301
00:20:40,385 --> 00:20:41,762
Go Eun-sae.

302
00:20:50,228 --> 00:20:51,897
No need to be flustered.

303
00:20:52,397 --> 00:20:53,899
Just do as I say from now on.

304
00:20:57,611 --> 00:20:58,862
Arms by your sides.

305
00:21:06,912 --> 00:21:08,205
Three steps back.

306
00:21:19,674 --> 00:21:21,134
You're dead meat.

307
00:21:30,268 --> 00:21:31,269
Excuse me.

308
00:21:32,938 --> 00:21:34,231
Your fly's open.

309
00:21:38,235 --> 00:21:42,322
I won't assume you're 100% faking
being drunk.

310
00:21:42,906 --> 00:21:47,077
But if you had enough sense
to zip up your damn fly,

311
00:21:48,537 --> 00:21:51,331
you shouldn't be grabbing
a taken man's hand.

312
00:22:00,507 --> 00:22:01,967
Your address.

313
00:22:03,135 --> 00:22:04,719
Jangmi Mansion.

314
00:22:04,803 --> 00:22:06,221
Jangmi Mansion?

315
00:22:06,721 --> 00:22:08,348
Okay.

316
00:22:10,225 --> 00:22:11,685
Hi, Gang-rok.

317
00:22:11,768 --> 00:22:14,604
You told me to think of you
as a little brother at my disposal,

318
00:22:14,688 --> 00:22:16,022
so do me a favor.

319
00:22:17,524 --> 00:22:19,818
There's a drunk lady over here.

320
00:22:20,402 --> 00:22:22,487
Please escort her home.

321
00:22:26,783 --> 00:22:27,617
How impressive.

322
00:22:50,015 --> 00:22:52,017
Impact detected.

323
00:22:55,479 --> 00:22:57,272
The car's nice, isn't it?

324
00:22:58,648 --> 00:23:01,735
The plastic wrap is still on.
Shall we tear it off together later?

325
00:23:01,818 --> 00:23:03,236
Forget the plastic wrap.

326
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:06,573
I wanted to tear out that girl's hair
but held myself back,

327
00:23:07,157 --> 00:23:08,575
so let's just go quietly.

328
00:23:25,425 --> 00:23:29,221
You know, I only held her up.

329
00:23:32,098 --> 00:23:33,475
So she wouldn't fall.

330
00:23:33,975 --> 00:23:36,144
If you face-plant on asphalt,

331
00:23:36,228 --> 00:23:38,772
you're in big trouble.
You could shatter your cheekbones.

332
00:23:38,855 --> 00:23:42,192
Why are that woman's cheekbones
any of your concern?

333
00:23:42,275 --> 00:23:43,109
Huh?

334
00:23:43,610 --> 00:23:45,862
It's as if you want to save
the entire world.

335
00:23:45,946 --> 00:23:48,198
Is it your dream to be an Avenger?

336
00:23:48,990 --> 00:23:50,951
Don't you know how to draw lines?

337
00:23:51,034 --> 00:23:53,995
You shouldn't have left her an opening.
You let her touch…

338
00:23:55,747 --> 00:23:58,750
Why would you let her touch you?

339
00:23:59,251 --> 00:24:02,379
Only I'm allowed to do that. Only me.

340
00:24:05,257 --> 00:24:06,091
You're smiling?

341
00:24:07,050 --> 00:24:08,134
Is this funny to you?

342
00:24:08,635 --> 00:24:12,430
Do you think
I'm being jealous or something?

343
00:24:12,514 --> 00:24:14,766
I'm talking about basic common sense here.

344
00:24:14,849 --> 00:24:17,018
Okay, it was wrong of me.

345
00:24:22,524 --> 00:24:23,775
I'm sorry.

346
00:24:26,611 --> 00:24:28,488
I'm serious.

347
00:24:29,072 --> 00:24:32,784
See what'll happen
if you ever touch another woman again.

348
00:24:34,369 --> 00:24:35,620
What's that?

349
00:24:36,204 --> 00:24:37,998
Some walnuts.

350
00:24:38,081 --> 00:24:40,458
They look like brains,
so they're brain food.

351
00:24:40,542 --> 00:24:42,294
To help you regain your memory.

352
00:24:43,753 --> 00:24:46,506
Come on, that's ridiculous.

353
00:24:46,590 --> 00:24:49,301
So, what, you drink milk
if you want fair skin

354
00:24:49,384 --> 00:24:52,137
and eat gochujang if you want red lips?

355
00:24:58,184 --> 00:24:59,352
What's wrong?

356
00:25:04,357 --> 00:25:05,567
Are you okay?

357
00:25:07,944 --> 00:25:09,321
I think

358
00:25:10,655 --> 00:25:11,990
I remember something.

359
00:25:16,953 --> 00:25:18,538
Go Ji-won!

360
00:25:19,289 --> 00:25:22,417
I said I'll make you eat gochujang
if you leave food, didn't I?

361
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:23,585
Eat it!

362
00:25:24,210 --> 00:25:26,379
Eat! I said eat!

363
00:25:26,463 --> 00:25:27,380
Open!

364
00:25:27,964 --> 00:25:30,592
Open your mouth! Wide! Open!

365
00:25:49,361 --> 00:25:50,570
Thank you.

366
00:25:55,241 --> 00:25:56,076
Feel better?

367
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,161
Yeah.

368
00:25:58,828 --> 00:26:01,498
I guess the treatment I got today worked.

369
00:26:02,332 --> 00:26:04,167
You remembered being at the orphanage?

370
00:26:05,293 --> 00:26:06,211
Yes.

371
00:26:07,379 --> 00:26:09,214
Not all of it,

372
00:26:10,090 --> 00:26:12,425
but bits and pieces, here and there.

373
00:26:15,261 --> 00:26:17,013
After I woke up with my memory gone,

374
00:26:17,097 --> 00:26:20,600
I really didn't want to go
to a government facility for some reason.

375
00:26:22,185 --> 00:26:23,728
Now I know why.

376
00:26:24,312 --> 00:26:25,980
I guess my body remembered.

377
00:26:26,064 --> 00:26:29,859
I told you to smile big
when they come to take pictures.

378
00:26:30,443 --> 00:26:33,780
At the orphanage,
we got group punishments all the time.

379
00:26:33,863 --> 00:26:34,781
Go Ji-won!

380
00:26:34,864 --> 00:26:37,951
In the middle of winter,
we were often kicked out barefoot.

381
00:26:38,034 --> 00:26:39,035
Outside.

382
00:26:40,912 --> 00:26:44,541
Just thinking about
how the cold crept into my feet…

383
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,502
It still gives me the chills.

384
00:26:50,004 --> 00:26:52,298
They abused you?

385
00:26:53,717 --> 00:26:57,554
Being kids without guardians
made us easy targets.

386
00:27:06,813 --> 00:27:10,191
And another thing.
We were dragged off to work.

387
00:27:11,651 --> 00:27:12,527
What?

388
00:27:12,610 --> 00:27:16,322
On weekends, we went to a rural area
about three hours away

389
00:27:16,406 --> 00:27:17,323
to work on a farm.

390
00:27:17,907 --> 00:27:21,244
I remember the trip to the country
being really rough.

391
00:27:21,327 --> 00:27:23,830
We were all crammed in a van

392
00:27:23,913 --> 00:27:25,039
for three hours.

393
00:27:25,540 --> 00:27:28,960
"Oh, I wish I could find
a discarded MP3 player or something."

394
00:27:29,043 --> 00:27:33,131
"Then I could listen to my favorite
god songs to help me get through it."

395
00:27:33,965 --> 00:27:36,342
I think I had innocent thoughts like that.

396
00:27:37,552 --> 00:27:40,263
Those things were a luxury
for kids like me.

397
00:27:47,228 --> 00:27:48,480
And

398
00:27:49,230 --> 00:27:52,817
there were also thugs
who took the orphanage's funds.

399
00:27:52,901 --> 00:27:55,153
When they got angry,

400
00:27:55,236 --> 00:27:59,908
they would beat up
the middle school boys at the orphanage.

401
00:28:00,408 --> 00:28:02,327
I was terrified.

402
00:28:04,078 --> 00:28:08,541
I guess that's why
I hate violence so much.

403
00:28:16,341 --> 00:28:18,176
What do you hate, Tae-ha?

404
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:21,805
What?

405
00:28:21,888 --> 00:28:25,517
I don't have any memories,
so I don't know much about you.

406
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:27,852
Tell me everything again, one by one.

407
00:28:27,936 --> 00:28:30,980
First off, your favorite things are
boxing and gochujang stew.

408
00:28:31,064 --> 00:28:33,191
Next, what don't you like?

409
00:28:38,196 --> 00:28:39,030
Rain.

410
00:28:39,781 --> 00:28:40,615
Rain?

411
00:28:42,408 --> 00:28:44,327
On the hardest days of my life,

412
00:28:44,828 --> 00:28:46,663
it always rained, for some reason.

413
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:54,712
BODEUM HOSPITAL CANCER CENTER

414
00:29:02,762 --> 00:29:04,681
Like the day Grandma collapsed…

415
00:29:08,685 --> 00:29:10,603
and the day I quit boxing.

416
00:29:11,229 --> 00:29:14,315
Just… days like those.

417
00:29:18,695 --> 00:29:22,824
TAEREUNG NATIONAL TRAINING CENTER

418
00:29:25,827 --> 00:29:27,579
In my bleakest moments,

419
00:29:28,288 --> 00:29:29,247
there was nothing

420
00:29:30,039 --> 00:29:32,166
to shield me from the rain.

421
00:29:33,376 --> 00:29:34,210
It felt like

422
00:29:35,336 --> 00:29:37,589
a reminder of just how hopeless
things were.

423
00:29:39,757 --> 00:29:40,925
So I don't like rain.

424
00:29:46,556 --> 00:29:48,766
I heard your story from Mr. Hong.

425
00:29:50,852 --> 00:29:53,771
Don't you regret
the decision you made back then?

426
00:29:54,939 --> 00:29:55,940
I don't.

427
00:29:56,733 --> 00:29:58,860
Because I protected
what I wanted to protect.

428
00:30:05,575 --> 00:30:06,492
Thank you.

429
00:30:09,037 --> 00:30:10,371
For protecting me too.

430
00:30:12,081 --> 00:30:13,958
If it had been anyone else,

431
00:30:15,668 --> 00:30:19,631
I think they would've given up on me
when I lost my memory and my mind.

432
00:30:25,929 --> 00:30:29,474
Now that I have some of my memories back,
I'm even more grateful to you.

433
00:30:31,851 --> 00:30:33,061
I'm glad

434
00:30:34,103 --> 00:30:36,064
that you're my boyfriend.

435
00:31:13,601 --> 00:31:14,560
I'm back!

436
00:31:15,478 --> 00:31:17,105
Right, yeah.

437
00:31:17,188 --> 00:31:18,231
Hello.

438
00:31:18,815 --> 00:31:21,234
-You're… here.
-Why do you have the lights off?

439
00:31:21,859 --> 00:31:23,444
I took the drunk lady home.

440
00:31:24,028 --> 00:31:27,323
I even rode the taxi with her
and saw her get inside safely.

441
00:31:28,825 --> 00:31:32,412
And on my way back, I saw someone
selling flower-shaped buns.

442
00:31:32,495 --> 00:31:33,329
Here.

443
00:31:34,956 --> 00:31:36,249
Would you like some?

444
00:31:40,003 --> 00:31:42,588
Buns at this hour?

445
00:31:42,672 --> 00:31:45,466
I ought to kick you in the buns.

446
00:31:45,967 --> 00:31:49,595
Yeah, eating them will only make you fat.
You're starting to get a belly.

447
00:31:53,099 --> 00:31:55,727
HONG'S BOXING GYM

448
00:31:58,438 --> 00:32:02,025
I got some nice sea bream at the market
and cooked it for you all.

449
00:32:02,108 --> 00:32:04,610
-I forgot water.
-I'll get it.

450
00:32:04,694 --> 00:32:05,611
No, please.

451
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,493
It's just that…

452
00:32:13,953 --> 00:32:15,788
Why would you let her touch you?

453
00:32:15,872 --> 00:32:18,458
Only I'm allowed to do that. Only me.

454
00:32:19,083 --> 00:32:22,211
I was told not to make
any physical contact with other women.

455
00:32:24,047 --> 00:32:24,964
What a load of crap.

456
00:32:25,965 --> 00:32:27,383
Are you out of your mind?

457
00:32:28,009 --> 00:32:30,970
Just leave him be.
He sure learned that well.

458
00:32:33,681 --> 00:32:34,515
Give that here.

459
00:32:36,184 --> 00:32:38,561
Eun-sae, will you be going
to the taffy shop today?

460
00:32:38,644 --> 00:32:40,146
The shop is closed today.

461
00:32:40,980 --> 00:32:42,565
Then shall we go to see the ritual?

462
00:32:43,191 --> 00:32:44,484
-The ritual?
-Yeah.

463
00:32:44,567 --> 00:32:46,694
Maeng-suk is performing
a shamanic ritual today.

464
00:32:47,195 --> 00:32:49,113
I see.

465
00:32:51,657 --> 00:32:53,034
Wait, I'm sorry.

466
00:32:53,534 --> 00:32:55,620
I forgot that I had something to do today.

467
00:32:56,329 --> 00:32:58,998
I was the one who suggested it,
but I'm flaking.

468
00:32:59,499 --> 00:33:02,126
I'll be back after a quick call.
Please go ahead.

469
00:33:02,210 --> 00:33:05,880
Why is he moving around so much
with that injured foot of his?

470
00:33:05,963 --> 00:33:07,381
Just leave him be.

471
00:33:09,092 --> 00:33:12,053
Wow, this soup is really something.

472
00:33:12,136 --> 00:33:13,096
Is it?

473
00:33:14,806 --> 00:33:16,015
That was delicious.

474
00:33:17,642 --> 00:33:18,810
You're leaving already?

475
00:33:20,311 --> 00:33:21,521
We finished eating.

476
00:33:22,271 --> 00:33:23,106
I'll get going.

477
00:33:23,689 --> 00:33:27,068
Okay. Remember to take your meds
and call if anything happens.

478
00:33:29,612 --> 00:33:31,322
See you later.

479
00:33:37,453 --> 00:33:39,205
Are you that happy?

480
00:33:44,335 --> 00:33:45,878
Why are you doing this?

481
00:33:45,962 --> 00:33:47,380
-Follow me quietly.
-Sorry?

482
00:33:47,463 --> 00:33:48,798
But, sir!

483
00:33:49,841 --> 00:33:51,050
My leg…

484
00:33:51,134 --> 00:33:53,219
Seriously, why are you doing this?

485
00:33:58,933 --> 00:34:02,728
Tell me. What are you up to?
Did Baek Sang-gil send you?

486
00:34:03,479 --> 00:34:06,482
No. Why would he send me?
I didn't even see his face when I left--

487
00:34:06,566 --> 00:34:07,900
Keep it down, damn it.

488
00:34:14,866 --> 00:34:17,034
Then who are you reporting to,
and about what?

489
00:34:17,660 --> 00:34:18,911
Where do you go at dawn?

490
00:34:18,995 --> 00:34:21,873
And why do you have two phones?
Explain it all. In detail.

491
00:34:31,757 --> 00:34:32,758
I…

492
00:34:37,430 --> 00:34:39,182
do YouTube live streams.

493
00:34:41,184 --> 00:34:44,020
-What?
-I review overseas soccer games.

494
00:34:44,604 --> 00:34:45,605
The phones.

495
00:34:47,481 --> 00:34:51,277
I have two because I watch soccer on one
while I film myself with the other.

496
00:34:51,861 --> 00:34:55,698
I've been leaving at dawn to stream
because that's when overseas games happen.

497
00:34:55,781 --> 00:34:58,367
I couldn't do it at home,
where you guys were sleeping.

498
00:34:58,451 --> 00:35:01,537
And he goes for it!
Up the field. On the other side!

499
00:35:02,413 --> 00:35:04,165
Oh, Ashley!

500
00:35:04,248 --> 00:35:06,209
This one's for you guys!

501
00:35:06,709 --> 00:35:07,835
Thank you!

502
00:35:09,462 --> 00:35:11,297
Guys, thank…

503
00:35:15,218 --> 00:35:16,636
I cover my face,

504
00:35:16,719 --> 00:35:20,556
and I avoid places that might give away
where we are, so you don't have to worry.

505
00:35:20,640 --> 00:35:23,267
And the calls are with my YouTube agency.

506
00:35:23,351 --> 00:35:25,061
They ask me when I can stream.

507
00:35:25,144 --> 00:35:27,438
The calls were me sharing my schedule.

508
00:35:28,773 --> 00:35:31,275
I quit the gang,
but I still needed to make a living.

509
00:35:32,026 --> 00:35:34,737
And my foot was like this.

510
00:35:34,820 --> 00:35:36,447
There was nothing I could do.

511
00:35:36,948 --> 00:35:40,368
So I asked myself,
"What was it that I truly liked?"

512
00:35:42,370 --> 00:35:44,497
"What did I want to become?"

513
00:35:46,499 --> 00:35:48,834
That's how I started doing this.

514
00:35:51,963 --> 00:35:54,507
If you don't believe me,
check for yourself.

515
00:36:11,274 --> 00:36:14,485
Hello, this is Studio Yes,
a YouTube content agency.

516
00:36:33,087 --> 00:36:34,338
Why is this so scuffed?

517
00:36:40,594 --> 00:36:42,013
When does the cast come off?

518
00:36:48,853 --> 00:36:52,064
I understand why you're so worried.

519
00:36:52,148 --> 00:36:55,609
Because if Chairman Baek…
I mean, if Baek Sang-gil finds out,

520
00:36:55,693 --> 00:36:58,654
neither you nor the prosecutor
will survive.

521
00:37:01,365 --> 00:37:03,284
The stowaway boat plan is getting close.

522
00:37:03,367 --> 00:37:04,910
Is the prosecutor getting better?

523
00:37:07,246 --> 00:37:09,123
Yesterday, she remembered her childhood.

524
00:37:09,749 --> 00:37:11,625
She'll likely regain her memory soon.

525
00:37:13,127 --> 00:37:14,795
I really hope that happens.

526
00:37:15,796 --> 00:37:19,967
If it does, it will be easier
to persuade her to leave the country,

527
00:37:21,052 --> 00:37:23,804
but wouldn't she also find out
that you're not her boyfriend?

528
00:37:25,473 --> 00:37:28,142
That would mean losing
the relationship you have now.

529
00:37:29,435 --> 00:37:31,354
Will you be okay with that?

530
00:37:35,649 --> 00:37:39,236
It doesn't matter what happens to me
as long as Go Eun-sae lives.

531
00:38:20,653 --> 00:38:22,696
-She's getting on the blades.
-She is!

532
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,698
It's so fascinating.

533
00:38:42,967 --> 00:38:44,760
What's taking her so long?

534
00:38:44,844 --> 00:38:46,846
-What's going on?
-She's not getting on.

535
00:38:46,929 --> 00:38:50,307
-Why isn't she getting on them?
-What's she doing?

536
00:38:55,146 --> 00:38:56,856
Hurry up already!

537
00:39:03,946 --> 00:39:06,073
Snake! It's a snake!

538
00:39:06,157 --> 00:39:07,366
-Snake?
-A snake?

539
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:09,368
A snake! There's a snake!

540
00:39:10,786 --> 00:39:11,829
What the heck?

541
00:39:11,912 --> 00:39:15,916
Isn't it bad luck to see snakes
or animal carcasses during a ritual?

542
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:19,044
Yeah, they say you shouldn't perform
a shamanic ritual if you see a snake.

543
00:39:19,128 --> 00:39:20,504
They say it won't work.

544
00:39:21,005 --> 00:39:22,756
It's no good if it won't work!

545
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:25,801
Then I guess we should call it a day.

546
00:39:27,928 --> 00:39:30,014
Hey, lady! Come down!

547
00:39:34,643 --> 00:39:35,561
Okay.

548
00:39:38,439 --> 00:39:39,523
Let's stop.

549
00:39:40,524 --> 00:39:42,276
Where did the snake even come from?

550
00:39:42,359 --> 00:39:43,611
Let's stop.

551
00:39:47,364 --> 00:39:49,033
I'm going to stop now!

552
00:39:49,867 --> 00:39:52,786
-She's stopping the ritual?
-She's stopping?

553
00:39:52,870 --> 00:39:54,121
Yes!

554
00:39:54,955 --> 00:39:56,916
I'm going to stop!

555
00:39:56,999 --> 00:39:57,875
What's wrong?

556
00:39:57,958 --> 00:39:59,293
What's going on?

557
00:40:01,587 --> 00:40:03,506
-What's going on?
-What's happening?

558
00:40:08,844 --> 00:40:10,179
What…

559
00:40:30,407 --> 00:40:31,575
I tried everything…

560
00:40:34,328 --> 00:40:36,747
but once the spirit leaves,
it doesn't come back.

561
00:40:40,334 --> 00:40:42,586
I'd been thinking about quitting
for a while,

562
00:40:42,670 --> 00:40:44,630
but I couldn't bring myself to do it.

563
00:40:44,713 --> 00:40:48,092
After losing my husband and child,
I only had my fortune-telling business.

564
00:40:48,175 --> 00:40:49,843
If I lost that too,

565
00:40:49,927 --> 00:40:52,346
my life would be too empty.

566
00:40:52,429 --> 00:40:54,723
What, are we just for show?

567
00:40:55,266 --> 00:40:58,310
You have us, two plump women,
under each of your arms.

568
00:40:58,894 --> 00:41:02,231
Why would your life be empty?

569
00:41:03,857 --> 00:41:06,360
That's why you should have
at least told us.

570
00:41:06,443 --> 00:41:10,906
This must have been gnawing at you
all this time…

571
00:41:13,117 --> 00:41:14,243
You guys are right.

572
00:41:14,326 --> 00:41:19,290
I'd briefly forgotten I had two ladies
who loomed large in my life.

573
00:41:24,336 --> 00:41:28,841
I feel so relieved, like I finally got
a whole load of old poop out of my system.

574
00:41:35,598 --> 00:41:36,765
As for you.

575
00:41:38,017 --> 00:41:39,435
Why did you help me?

576
00:41:44,273 --> 00:41:46,066
Well, I had no other choice.

577
00:41:46,817 --> 00:41:50,738
If I had left you alone,
your feet would've been covered in blood.

578
00:41:53,365 --> 00:41:56,660
I guess you're not a total lost cause.

579
00:41:59,204 --> 00:42:03,500
Well, I realized something
after losing my memory.

580
00:42:04,501 --> 00:42:07,379
I had something,
but it disappeared overnight.

581
00:42:07,463 --> 00:42:09,673
I was flustered

582
00:42:09,757 --> 00:42:11,759
and bitter.

583
00:42:12,343 --> 00:42:14,345
It all felt unfair.

584
00:42:15,512 --> 00:42:17,973
But what I lost wouldn't come back.

585
00:42:18,891 --> 00:42:21,727
My emotions were all over the place
dozens of times a day.

586
00:42:21,810 --> 00:42:24,146
It drove me to the brink of insanity.

587
00:42:25,648 --> 00:42:30,611
Then it occurred to me
that you must have felt the same way.

588
00:42:32,780 --> 00:42:34,156
You two were in the same boat?

589
00:42:35,157 --> 00:42:36,116
I guess.

590
00:42:36,784 --> 00:42:38,410
Life is funny, isn't it?

591
00:42:38,494 --> 00:42:41,246
Just the other day
you were fighting over a broken statue.

592
00:42:42,706 --> 00:42:46,919
Who'd have thought that you two
would now be seeing eye to eye?

593
00:42:47,461 --> 00:42:48,754
Tell me about it.

594
00:42:49,254 --> 00:42:51,632
Let's have a drink,
since we see eye to eye.

595
00:42:51,715 --> 00:42:52,633
Cheers!

596
00:42:53,634 --> 00:42:55,052
Let us join in.

597
00:42:56,428 --> 00:42:57,262
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

598
00:42:57,346 --> 00:42:58,889
Oh, great spirit!

599
00:42:58,972 --> 00:43:04,728
Never come looking for me again

600
00:43:04,812 --> 00:43:08,107
Don't you dare curse me

601
00:43:08,190 --> 00:43:11,819
For being a cruel woman…

602
00:43:12,444 --> 00:43:16,824
I love you to death

603
00:43:16,907 --> 00:43:20,577
Why don't you believe me?

604
00:43:20,661 --> 00:43:23,372
Until the day I die

605
00:43:23,455 --> 00:43:26,709
You're the only one for me

606
00:43:26,792 --> 00:43:31,463
Actually, no, even if I die

607
00:43:31,547 --> 00:43:34,717
You'd still be the only one for me

608
00:43:34,800 --> 00:43:38,303
So please open your heart, believe me

609
00:43:38,387 --> 00:43:40,013
And love me

610
00:43:40,097 --> 00:43:42,474
I love you, ladies!

611
00:43:42,558 --> 00:43:43,767
Careful.

612
00:43:44,309 --> 00:43:48,564
You sexy man, you're my man

613
00:43:48,647 --> 00:43:52,651
You handsome man, you're my man

614
00:43:52,735 --> 00:43:55,696
When this world ends
I'll lose myself in a fantasy

615
00:43:55,779 --> 00:43:57,990
Why did you make her drink so much?

616
00:43:58,073 --> 00:43:59,658
-What?
-Hey!

617
00:44:00,242 --> 00:44:03,912
No, we didn't make her drink.

618
00:44:03,996 --> 00:44:06,623
Your wifey did it all by herself.

619
00:44:09,126 --> 00:44:10,544
It was yummy.

620
00:44:11,170 --> 00:44:13,922
Your wifey is approved! Approved by us!

621
00:44:14,006 --> 00:44:15,007
Approved!

622
00:44:15,090 --> 00:44:16,759
Ladies, let's go for a third round!

623
00:44:16,842 --> 00:44:18,218
-Let's go.
-Sounds good!

624
00:44:18,302 --> 00:44:21,722
Then should we go to the club in town
with the roof that opens?

625
00:44:21,805 --> 00:44:22,806
Let's go!

626
00:44:22,890 --> 00:44:25,225
What are you talking about?
Please get home safely.

627
00:44:25,309 --> 00:44:26,477
Let's go!

628
00:44:26,560 --> 00:44:29,062
My sexy man

629
00:44:29,146 --> 00:44:30,856
-Let's get you home.
-I want to go!

630
00:44:31,857 --> 00:44:34,568
-I can drink more.
-No, you'll die if you drink more.

631
00:44:45,204 --> 00:44:47,206
Hey, it's my boyfriend,

632
00:44:47,915 --> 00:44:49,249
Jang Tae-ha.

633
00:44:50,667 --> 00:44:51,543
Go to sleep.

634
00:44:53,295 --> 00:44:54,421
Okay.

635
00:44:54,505 --> 00:44:58,217
But don't go anywhere

636
00:44:59,134 --> 00:45:00,552
until I fall asleep.

637
00:45:02,638 --> 00:45:03,472
Okay.

638
00:45:46,974 --> 00:45:48,851
If she remembers everything,

639
00:45:48,934 --> 00:45:51,937
that would mean losing
the relationship you have now.

640
00:45:52,729 --> 00:45:54,648
Will you be okay with that?

641
00:46:20,215 --> 00:46:23,093
I'm told that multiple guys
have seen Prosecutor Go.

642
00:46:23,969 --> 00:46:25,012
They saw Go Ji-won?

643
00:46:25,095 --> 00:46:27,431
At first, I also thought
it was impossible, but…

644
00:46:27,514 --> 00:46:29,808
-Hey.
-What is it?

645
00:46:29,892 --> 00:46:31,226
Isn't that Prosecutor Go?

646
00:46:33,020 --> 00:46:35,856
Even though they saw her
at different locations,

647
00:46:35,939 --> 00:46:38,567
their descriptions of her outfit
were identical.

648
00:46:43,280 --> 00:46:45,824
Given the circumstances,
I thought I should tell you first.

649
00:46:58,587 --> 00:47:00,339
If it really is Go Ji-won,

650
00:47:00,839 --> 00:47:02,633
does that mean Jang Tae-ha lost her?

651
00:47:07,304 --> 00:47:08,180
That,

652
00:47:09,097 --> 00:47:10,807
or he let her live.

653
00:47:14,895 --> 00:47:16,104
Impossible.

654
00:47:17,314 --> 00:47:20,567
Sir, what's more worrying
is what Gwak Chi-hyeon said.

655
00:47:20,651 --> 00:47:24,321
Prosecutor Go said she had prepared
one more thing besides the watch.

656
00:47:24,905 --> 00:47:27,115
If Prosecutor Go really is alive,

657
00:47:27,658 --> 00:47:29,409
it's suspicious that she's been quiet.

658
00:47:30,619 --> 00:47:34,206
She could be preparing something
with what Gwak Chi-hyeon mentioned.

659
00:47:49,596 --> 00:47:51,264
My stomach's killing me.

660
00:47:51,974 --> 00:47:53,809
How much did I drink last night?

661
00:47:58,355 --> 00:48:00,691
This is my boyfriend.

662
00:48:00,774 --> 00:48:03,276
He studied international relations
at Hanguk University

663
00:48:03,360 --> 00:48:04,987
and is now the Gangju mayor's aide.

664
00:48:05,070 --> 00:48:06,780
Nice to meet you. I'm Gwak Chi-hyeon.

665
00:48:09,241 --> 00:48:11,451
What… is this?

666
00:48:12,119 --> 00:48:13,578
What is this memory?

667
00:48:14,663 --> 00:48:16,289
He's my boyfriend?

668
00:48:16,373 --> 00:48:17,916
Is he an ex-boyfriend?

669
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:22,045
I've heard a lot about you from the mayor.
I look forward to your support.

670
00:48:22,129 --> 00:48:23,338
No, it's recent.

671
00:48:23,422 --> 00:48:26,425
-Did you say we dated for two years?
-Yeah.

672
00:48:27,551 --> 00:48:29,011
What is this?

673
00:48:34,641 --> 00:48:35,976
Did you get some sleep?

674
00:48:37,102 --> 00:48:38,311
Is your stomach okay?

675
00:48:40,147 --> 00:48:41,064
Yes.

676
00:48:46,361 --> 00:48:48,864
By any chance,

677
00:48:49,364 --> 00:48:50,699
did I…

678
00:48:51,450 --> 00:48:52,451
Yes?

679
00:48:57,622 --> 00:48:58,623
Never mind.

680
00:49:03,503 --> 00:49:05,505
-You remembered that?
-Yes.

681
00:49:06,006 --> 00:49:07,466
But it doesn't make sense.

682
00:49:07,549 --> 00:49:09,718
I've been dating Jang Tae-ha
for two years.

683
00:49:09,801 --> 00:49:13,555
Why would I introduce someone
named Gwak Chi-hyeon as my boyfriend?

684
00:49:14,056 --> 00:49:15,307
So I was wondering,

685
00:49:15,390 --> 00:49:18,393
could this be a memory of a dream
or something I imagined?

686
00:49:20,479 --> 00:49:23,023
I'm not sure.
It's not completely impossible.

687
00:49:23,106 --> 00:49:25,233
But there's no way to be sure.

688
00:49:26,860 --> 00:49:27,903
Wait a minute.

689
00:49:29,446 --> 00:49:30,947
Actually, there might be a way.

690
00:49:32,574 --> 00:49:35,702
-How?
-Didn't you say he studied at Hanguk Uni?

691
00:49:35,786 --> 00:49:39,039
-Yes.
-I went to med school there!

692
00:49:39,122 --> 00:49:40,040
Look behind you.

693
00:49:40,123 --> 00:49:41,374
Hold on, one second.

694
00:49:41,875 --> 00:49:44,294
Let me check with a friend
who was in that department.

695
00:49:44,377 --> 00:49:45,545
DIRECTOR AN GI-JUN

696
00:49:45,629 --> 00:49:48,090
HANGUK UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF MEDICINE

697
00:49:58,141 --> 00:50:00,435
CHAIRMAN BAEK SANG-GIL

698
00:50:06,733 --> 00:50:07,567
How did it go?

699
00:50:07,651 --> 00:50:11,404
They're yet to find CCTV footage
of the person they think is Prosecutor Go.

700
00:50:11,488 --> 00:50:14,908
If that bitch really is alive,
we don't have time to waste like this.

701
00:50:15,575 --> 00:50:17,285
Find her in two days, no matter what.

702
00:50:19,621 --> 00:50:20,914
How did it go?

703
00:50:23,375 --> 00:50:24,209
Unbelievable.

704
00:50:24,292 --> 00:50:27,796
There really was a guy named
Gwak Chi-hyeon in that department.

705
00:50:29,047 --> 00:50:30,465
And… Take a seat.

706
00:50:34,553 --> 00:50:36,388
My friend gave me his number.

707
00:50:36,471 --> 00:50:37,639
So,

708
00:50:38,181 --> 00:50:39,975
do you want to find out

709
00:50:41,143 --> 00:50:42,144
if your memory is real?

710
00:50:46,898 --> 00:50:48,900
SEOUN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

711
00:50:53,405 --> 00:50:54,698
Please, can you stop…

712
00:50:56,199 --> 00:50:58,118
Can you please stop tailing me?

713
00:50:58,827 --> 00:51:02,330
I got fired from my job as an aide.
What could I do in this state…

714
00:51:10,714 --> 00:51:12,549
-Hello?
-Is this Mr. Gwak Chi-hyeon?

715
00:51:12,632 --> 00:51:13,592
Yes, it is.

716
00:51:13,675 --> 00:51:15,927
This is Go Ji-won.

717
00:51:16,011 --> 00:51:17,012
Ji-won?

718
00:51:18,263 --> 00:51:19,806
Hey, Ji-won.

719
00:51:19,890 --> 00:51:20,891
Where are you?

720
00:51:20,974 --> 00:51:24,269
Why haven't you been answering my calls?
Where are you?

721
00:51:27,564 --> 00:51:29,399
I'll explain the details

722
00:51:30,317 --> 00:51:31,276
in person.

723
00:51:31,943 --> 00:51:33,820
Sure. Where should we meet?

724
00:51:33,904 --> 00:51:34,946
Where would be good?

725
00:51:35,530 --> 00:51:36,573
In Seoul.

726
00:51:38,825 --> 00:51:41,328
Tonight, in Seoul.

727
00:51:41,411 --> 00:51:43,538
Okay, let's do that. All right.

728
00:51:46,917 --> 00:51:48,418
A clinic in Seoul?

729
00:51:48,501 --> 00:51:49,336
Yeah.

730
00:51:49,419 --> 00:51:53,715
Since some of her memory has returned,
I thought we could give it a boost

731
00:51:53,798 --> 00:51:56,885
by trying
a more sophisticated form of TMS.

732
00:51:56,968 --> 00:51:58,386
My friend runs a clinic,

733
00:51:58,470 --> 00:52:01,264
and they recently bought
an upgraded TMS machine.

734
00:52:01,348 --> 00:52:02,557
Of course we should go.

735
00:52:02,641 --> 00:52:03,975
When can we go?

736
00:52:04,851 --> 00:52:05,685
Tonight.

737
00:52:06,353 --> 00:52:08,021
-Tonight?
-Yeah.

738
00:52:08,104 --> 00:52:12,275
They're fully booked for a while,
so today is the only open slot.

739
00:52:13,235 --> 00:52:14,319
Let's go.

740
00:52:17,656 --> 00:52:19,866
But you have a lesson tonight.

741
00:52:19,950 --> 00:52:21,618
I can just reschedule it.

742
00:52:21,701 --> 00:52:25,330
I just happen to have a seminar
in Seoul today.

743
00:52:25,413 --> 00:52:28,083
I'm going to Seoul,
so I can take Ms. Go with me.

744
00:52:28,166 --> 00:52:30,210
-No need to go out of your way.
-It's fine.

745
00:52:31,503 --> 00:52:32,504
One second.

746
00:52:35,882 --> 00:52:37,259
Why is she calling me?

747
00:52:37,342 --> 00:52:38,551
KIM SONG-WOL

748
00:52:40,178 --> 00:52:41,012
Yes?

749
00:52:47,727 --> 00:52:49,145
Grandma!

750
00:52:50,313 --> 00:52:51,398
Grandma!

751
00:52:51,481 --> 00:52:52,357
Grandma!

752
00:52:52,857 --> 00:52:54,442
-Ma'am?
-What's wrong?

753
00:52:54,526 --> 00:52:56,403
Grandma, what's wrong? What is it?

754
00:52:56,903 --> 00:52:57,779
What?

755
00:53:04,119 --> 00:53:07,247
DEPARTMENT OF NUCLEAR MEDICINE
PET-CT SCAN ROOM

756
00:53:29,227 --> 00:53:30,437
She has a tumor.

757
00:53:32,063 --> 00:53:33,398
If it's malignant,

758
00:53:33,481 --> 00:53:35,817
can she get surgery like last time?

759
00:53:35,900 --> 00:53:40,905
Well, her body is much weaker
than it was 14 years ago,

760
00:53:41,740 --> 00:53:43,408
so it would be more complicated.

761
00:53:44,576 --> 00:53:47,871
Let's wait for the test results first.

762
00:53:50,457 --> 00:53:51,291
Okay.

763
00:54:08,641 --> 00:54:10,894
I think I should stay with Grandma today.

764
00:54:10,977 --> 00:54:12,937
You should go to Seoul with Gi-jun.

765
00:54:13,813 --> 00:54:15,940
No, I'll go next time.

766
00:54:16,983 --> 00:54:19,652
You should go. Today's your only chance.

767
00:54:20,570 --> 00:54:23,698
Your treatment
is as important to me as Grandma.

768
00:54:23,782 --> 00:54:25,617
Grandma would want that too.

769
00:54:42,467 --> 00:54:44,219
-Thanks.
-It's nothing.

770
00:54:45,804 --> 00:54:48,098
These are your meds. Take them on time.

771
00:54:50,975 --> 00:54:51,851
I'll be back.

772
00:54:51,935 --> 00:54:53,853
Wait. Can you wait just a little?

773
00:54:53,937 --> 00:54:55,105
Mr. Hong's coming.

774
00:54:55,188 --> 00:54:56,064
What?

775
00:54:57,607 --> 00:54:58,858
Why is he coming?

776
00:54:58,942 --> 00:55:00,485
I asked him to go with you.

777
00:55:00,568 --> 00:55:03,905
You have your seminar.
Someone should take care of Eun-sae.

778
00:55:03,988 --> 00:55:06,741
There's no need.
I don't want to go with a stranger, okay?

779
00:55:06,825 --> 00:55:08,785
-We'll be fine.
-Yes.

780
00:55:09,369 --> 00:55:12,580
I don't want Mr. Hong
rescheduling his lessons for me.

781
00:55:13,206 --> 00:55:15,625
-Still…
-I won't leave her alone.

782
00:55:15,708 --> 00:55:17,502
Don't worry. See you when we get back.

783
00:55:20,380 --> 00:55:22,340
Hey, Gi-jun.

784
00:55:23,550 --> 00:55:24,509
Yes, Doctor?

785
00:55:25,009 --> 00:55:26,094
Has my grandma woken up?

786
00:55:44,195 --> 00:55:46,656
This is Go Ji-won.

787
00:55:46,739 --> 00:55:47,782
Ji-won?

788
00:55:47,866 --> 00:55:49,409
Hey, Ji-won.

789
00:55:49,492 --> 00:55:51,995
Where are you?
Why haven't you been answering my calls?

790
00:55:52,078 --> 00:55:53,705
I'll explain the details

791
00:55:54,581 --> 00:55:56,249
in person.

792
00:56:11,723 --> 00:56:12,849
Let's say

793
00:56:13,475 --> 00:56:18,229
this man called Gwak Chi-hyeon
really is your boyfriend.

794
00:56:18,813 --> 00:56:19,689
What then?

795
00:56:23,693 --> 00:56:25,487
If that's the case,

796
00:56:25,570 --> 00:56:28,448
it would be one of two things.

797
00:56:28,948 --> 00:56:32,285
Either Jang Tae-ha's fake,
or I was two-timing.

798
00:56:34,412 --> 00:56:35,747
Whatever the case,

799
00:56:36,539 --> 00:56:38,541
I think I'll be really sad.

800
00:56:59,729 --> 00:57:00,563
Grandma.

801
00:57:01,356 --> 00:57:02,190
Yeah?

802
00:57:03,441 --> 00:57:04,275
What?

803
00:57:05,193 --> 00:57:06,027
Are you okay?

804
00:57:09,155 --> 00:57:11,950
Am I… sick?

805
00:57:16,037 --> 00:57:17,205
We don't know yet.

806
00:57:18,039 --> 00:57:20,083
We have to wait for the test results.

807
00:57:20,166 --> 00:57:21,834
Don't you worry.

808
00:57:22,544 --> 00:57:24,712
I won't die that easily.

809
00:57:25,672 --> 00:57:30,134
After everything you did to save my life,
how could I possibly…

810
00:57:31,928 --> 00:57:37,058
I'm going to hold on tight and protect it.

811
00:57:39,811 --> 00:57:40,812
You promise?

812
00:57:40,895 --> 00:57:42,647
Yes, of course.

813
00:57:48,403 --> 00:57:51,656
Don't you know how strong I am?

814
00:57:54,033 --> 00:57:57,787
No matter how hard the disease
tries to get me,

815
00:57:58,746 --> 00:58:00,873
it won't stand a chance against me.

816
00:58:01,374 --> 00:58:02,500
No way.

817
00:58:15,722 --> 00:58:17,307
My precious baby.

818
00:58:19,809 --> 00:58:21,311
My absolute blessing.

819
00:58:27,734 --> 00:58:29,444
I'm going to be fine.

820
00:58:30,445 --> 00:58:33,865
You should go home and sleep comfortably.

821
00:58:34,907 --> 00:58:36,117
Okay?

822
00:58:39,037 --> 00:58:39,996
Go on home.

823
00:58:41,205 --> 00:58:42,040
Go on.

824
00:58:43,791 --> 00:58:46,044
I'm going to get some sleep.

825
00:58:46,127 --> 00:58:47,295
Go on home.

826
00:59:32,715 --> 00:59:35,218
BODEUM HOSPITAL CANCER CENTER

827
01:00:13,381 --> 01:00:14,257
Go Eun-sae.

828
01:00:14,966 --> 01:00:15,800
You…

829
01:00:16,300 --> 01:00:18,052
What happened to you?

830
01:00:19,137 --> 01:00:20,179
What about the treatment?

831
01:00:30,732 --> 01:00:31,733
Time for my meds.

832
01:00:41,117 --> 01:00:44,871
In the middle of winter,
we were often kicked out barefoot.

833
01:00:45,371 --> 01:00:49,500
Just thinking about
how the cold crept into my feet…

834
01:00:50,376 --> 01:00:51,711
It still gives me the chills.

835
01:01:08,728 --> 01:01:12,940
Turns out MP3 players are still around.
Listen to this if you get carsick.

836
01:01:14,317 --> 01:01:17,737
"Oh, I wish I could find
a discarded MP3 player or something."

837
01:01:17,820 --> 01:01:22,408
"Then I could listen to my favorite
god songs to help me get through it."

838
01:01:22,492 --> 01:01:25,119
Those things were a luxury
for kids like me.

839
01:01:27,121 --> 01:01:29,373
01. GOD - ONE CANDLE
02. GOD - LOVE YOU AND…

840
01:01:30,708 --> 01:01:32,460
Jang Tae-ha, you…

841
01:01:36,589 --> 01:01:38,466
What's wrong? Did you remember something?

842
01:01:41,177 --> 01:01:42,011
What the…

843
01:01:43,679 --> 01:01:45,640
Right, rain's forecast nationwide tonight.

844
01:01:47,934 --> 01:01:49,352
Doctor,

845
01:01:49,852 --> 01:01:51,103
let's just go back.

846
01:01:51,187 --> 01:01:52,230
What?

847
01:01:55,525 --> 01:01:57,401
I need to go back.

848
01:01:58,027 --> 01:01:59,362
What are you talking about?

849
01:01:59,445 --> 01:02:02,073
You're just going back
without even checking the facts?

850
01:02:04,867 --> 01:02:07,078
This can't be fake.

851
01:02:09,705 --> 01:02:11,707
Jang Tae-ha is real.

852
01:02:12,792 --> 01:02:14,836
So let's just go back.

853
01:02:17,839 --> 01:02:20,675
I want to go to Tae-ha right now.

854
01:02:27,473 --> 01:02:30,434
I asked about your treatment.
Did you get it already?

855
01:02:33,396 --> 01:02:35,231
If I said that I was more worried about

856
01:02:36,899 --> 01:02:39,569
you getting caught in the rain
than recovering my memory…

857
01:02:42,822 --> 01:02:43,906
would you believe me?

858
01:02:46,325 --> 01:02:48,286
Even if I can't do much else for you,

859
01:02:48,870 --> 01:02:51,080
on hard days like tonight,

860
01:02:53,040 --> 01:02:56,043
I thought I could at least shield you
from the rain.

861
01:02:58,880 --> 01:03:00,673
I really wanted to do that for you.

862
01:03:04,176 --> 01:03:05,845
In my bleakest moments,

863
01:03:05,928 --> 01:03:08,973
there was nothing
to shield me from the rain.

864
01:03:09,056 --> 01:03:11,893
It felt like a reminder
of just how hopeless things were.

865
01:03:12,393 --> 01:03:13,352
So I don't like rain.

866
01:03:22,820 --> 01:03:24,614
Let's weather it together from now on.

867
01:03:29,243 --> 01:03:30,870
I'll be with you.

868
01:04:36,936 --> 01:04:38,604
OUR STICKY LOVE

869
01:05:25,234 --> 01:05:29,196
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

